{"title":"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Recursion)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Recursion)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a> is called <i>parity-monotonic</i> if its decimal representation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49ef1280a5790f9905856915237bde01c3ffbbdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}a_{2}a_{3}\\cdots a_{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"10\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33d11750c9041bf6b25499e6717ea911857aa720.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i}&lt;a_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a772bd794fbedb2976268c491686644aefc02e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Odd\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Odd\">odd</a>, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae5095b90d2ad1a701d0ffb01fb336ee9916ce7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i}&gt;a_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a772bd794fbedb2976268c491686644aefc02e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Even\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Even\">even</a>. How many four-digit parity-monotonic integers are there?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's set up a table of values. Notice that 0 and 9 both cannot appear as any of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/5/7d5f459277637a6a42172ee02751ed011606a817.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,\\ a_2,\\ a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"11\" /> because of the given conditions. (Also note that 0 cannot appear as 0 cannot be the first digit of an integer.) A clear pattern emerges.\n</p><p>For example, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the second column, we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/3/48313226ddd5072b0b85f2fe57a25b908696c319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,6,8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, but greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so there are four possible places to align <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as the second digit.\n</p>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Digit&#160;&#160;</td>\n<td>1st&#160;&#160;</td>\n<td>2nd&#160;&#160;</td>\n<td>3rd&#160;&#160;</td>\n<td>4th\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>64\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>64\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>64\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>64\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>64\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>64\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>64\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>64\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>16</td>\n<td>64\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>0</td>\n<td>64\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>For any number from 1-8, there are exactly 4 numbers from 1-8 that are odd and less than the number or that are even and greater than the number (the same will happen for 0 and 9 in the last column). Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/c/b0c269eca189b250fc8281b3e3c27bbedc822867.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{k-1} \\cdot 10 = 4^3\\cdot10 = 640$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"188\" height=\"16\" />.\n-yeetdayeet\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Recursion.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Recursion)\">Solution 2 (Recursion)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Recursion)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This problem can be solved via recursion since we are \"building a string\" of numbers with some condition. We want to create a new string by adding a new digit at the front so we avoid complications (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can't be at the front and no digit is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />). There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> options to add no matter what<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae94730216adbc031bd00b320b68f45d9e1aed4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{\\ast}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae94730216adbc031bd00b320b68f45d9e1aed4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{\\ast}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae94730216adbc031bd00b320b68f45d9e1aed4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{\\ast}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"15\" /> so the recursion is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/9/c59b78baec8c140d1950d3adc4f8dc831d81b2f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n=4S_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a070eea97d9363f58a257e05e75fc69efa753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> stands for the number of such numbers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> digits. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec73f7522870432d751b3e0356de91edb74f3d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed3a7df3824d42274e82684164e0d967412c1ab1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{640}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae94730216adbc031bd00b320b68f45d9e1aed4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{\\ast}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae94730216adbc031bd00b320b68f45d9e1aed4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{\\ast}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae94730216adbc031bd00b320b68f45d9e1aed4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^{\\ast}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"15\" /> divide 0-9 into groups <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/3/4e349146e926f0647c2de71b6d0df587e1fef982.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(E O)(E O)(E O)(E O)(E O)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"217\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is even, take an odd from a group below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />'s group or an even from a group above its group as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc11a89db6e73586cd50c302b05c7c4c041dc464.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"30\" height=\"10\" />. Do the opposite for an odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. So for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> there is one option for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc11a89db6e73586cd50c302b05c7c4c041dc464.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"30\" height=\"10\" /> from each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> groups that are not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />'s group.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/BgcMhhTZfqM?si=TcYTatHHqxaq1NgT\">2007 AIME II #6</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://mathproblemsolvingskills.wordpress.com/\">MathProblemSolvingSkills.com</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II\" title=\"2007 AIME II\">2007 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2007\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2007 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017063005\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 259/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6206/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.321      1 -total\n 58.28%    7.181      1 Template:AIME_box\n 40.01%    4.929      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4806:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017063005 and revision id 289868. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}